[317.670368, "o", "Done. Here's the summary.\r\n\r\n## Found & recorded — 3 papers\r\n\r\nAll three identified unambiguously on Semantic Scholar (top hit each), DOIs verified via CrossRef, and pushed to your personal Zotero library:\r\n\r\n| Citation key | Paper | DOI | Zotero key |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `@Yan2016dpabi` | DPABI: Data Processing & Analysis for (Resting-State) Brain Imaging (Neuroinformatics, 2016) | `10.1007/s12021-016-9299-4` | `AEFCB5G7` |\r\n| `@Hallquist2013nuisance` | The Nuisance of Nuisance Regression: Spectral Misspecification… (NeuroImage, 2013) | `10.1016/j.neuroimage.2013.05.116` | `PXAT9XFV` |\r\n| `@Nietocastanon2020handbook` | Handbook of functional connectivity MRI methods in CONN (Hilbert Press, 2020) | `10.56441/hilbertpress.2207.6598` | `9GTKQEAM` |\r\n\r\n- Written to `references/library.json` (new file; this demo dir had no `references/` setup, so I scaffolded a minimal `references/zotero.yaml` → personal library, no collection).\r\n- `last_sync` stamped `2026-06-05T17:06:39Z`.\r\n\r\n## Two things to flag honestly\r\n\r\n1. **The \"dry-run\" wasn't a preview.** I placed `--dry-run` before the `add` subcommand, but that subcommand doesn't inherit the global flag — so the very first call **executed for real** and pushed all three to Zotero. The end state is exactly what you asked for, so no harm, but it ran live rather than as the preview I intended.\r\n\r\n2. **I did the push half of \"sync\" but not a pull.** The `add` path records locally + pushes to Zotero. I deliberately did **not** run a full `pull`, because with no collection set, a pull would download your entire personal Zotero library into this `tmp/minidemo/library.json` — almost certainly not what you want in a demo dir.\r\n\r\nWant me to either (a) set a target **collection** in `references/zotero.yaml` and run a proper scoped `sync`, or (b) leave it as-is with just these three recorded?\r\n"]
